# Commits

When the user asks to commit or push, create the commit locally with their existing git identity.

- Do not add `Co-authored-by`, `Signed-off-by`, or any other trailer that names the agent or another author.
- Do not change `git config`. Author and committer both stay the name and email already configured in this repository.
- Do not open a pull request, use the GitHub web UI, or use a cloud agent to land the change.
- After committing, check `git log -1 --format=full`. If a co-author trailer is present, replace that unpushed commit before pushing.
